      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The factor \\( \\left(1 + \\sin(4x)\\right)^{2} \\) is a square of \\( 1 + \\sin(4x) \\), which contains a sine of \\( 4x \\), so apply the chain rule from the outside inward: \\( \\left(\\left(1 + \\sin(4x)\\right)^{2}\\right)' = 8 \\left(\\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 1\\right) \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
